   *  A producer MUST NOT classify a claim as EMPIRICALLY_EVIDENCED
      without a validated observation or measurement binding appropriate
      to the scope.

   *  A SOURCE_BOUND claim MUST NOT be promoted to object truth solely
      because the source is present, authoritative, popular, or
      cryptographically identified.

   *  A PREDICTED claim MUST NOT be represented as OBSERVED merely
      because an execution completed successfully.

   *  A historical PASS MUST NOT be represented as a current PASS for a
      changed subject unless an explicit invariance relation justifies
      the transfer.

   *  The same rules MUST apply to claims previously emitted by the
      cognition system itself.

5.  Claim Binding

   A deployment profile MUST bind at least claim identifier, subject
   identity, subject state or version where applicable, observation
   time, evidence references, source identity, and epistemic status.  A
   deployment SHOULD also bind the evaluator and applicable policy
   version.

   claim = (
     claim_id,
     subject,
     subject_state,
     observed_at,
     evidence_refs,
     source_refs,
     evaluator,
     policy_version,
     epistemic_status
   )

6.  Relationship to EFFECT_ACK

   This profile does not change the QIK-VRT EFFECT_ACK five-state
   version-1 contract.  EFFECT_ACK determines whether a downstream
   effect is authorized under a bound policy and evidence set.  This
   profile determines which epistemic status may be asserted for a
   claim.






